# Phase 3, 7.2: CSI-2 link stress of the 319.2 MHz PLL variants (stock, V0, V1, V2, V3)

Machine: esteban, Surface Book 2 13" (i7-8650U), OV7251 infrared sensor on ipu3-cio2. Kernel: 7.2.12-gcov. Date: 2026-10-27T20:50:59+09:00. Operator: Claude (subagent), driven by tools/link-stress.py and the K9 reload procedure from tests/test_k9_reload.py.

Variants of the 19.2 MHz external clock -> 319.2 MHz link frequency table (ov7251_pll1_cfg_19_2_mhz_319_2_mhz) in the project's converted driver kernel/backport/ov7251.c (the v2 series): V0 = kernel/backport/ov7251.c unchanged, mainline PLL1 values (pre_div 0x01, mult 0x85, div 0x04, pix_div 0x0a, mipi_div 0x05, three { 0x4837, 0x19 } mode-table entries), built as /tmp/claude-1000/-home-antoine-projects-surface/3ccf287b-d9c6-4190-a42c-0b614d1d1d83/scratchpad/variants/V0/ov7251.ko (sha256 0e4c1e7a146c87a7ef6b14bdb74110dd17f74ba09182ed3ec2a67c2ac0d728cb); V1 = V0 with .pre_div = 0x04 (was 0x01) and .div = 0x01 (was 0x04) in that one initializer and nothing else, the Windows Hello dividers, same 638.4 Mbps output with the PLL oscillator at 638.4 MHz, /tmp/claude-1000/-home-antoine-projects-surface/3ccf287b-d9c6-4190-a42c-0b614d1d1d83/scratchpad/variants/V1/ov7251.ko (sha256 96d96e221cc0a94b449db7aa489899d1c2b57b5317c222c2a3fa8bb759f967d0); V2 = V1 plus the three mode-table entries { 0x4837, 0x19 } changed to { 0x4837, 0x1f } (MIPI global timing), /tmp/claude-1000/-home-antoine-projects-surface/3ccf287b-d9c6-4190-a42c-0b614d1d1d83/scratchpad/variants/V2/ov7251.ko (sha256 b7837cb6d759fcfa67c5361238ca18576049ddad179d15580a4ac4a86484eea9); stock = the in-kernel module /lib/modules/7.2.12-gcov/kernel/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.ko (sha256 7954b1d84cd65a2941cc961cc3e87cd1463fdb85a200b4b2ee8c7bc96d083c86), mainline 7.2's driver, which always runs the 240 MHz table because of the link-frequency index bug that patch 1 of the series fixes. All four report vermagic "7.2.12-gcov SMP preempt mod_unload ". The three variants were built against /home/antoine/build/kernel-gcov/kernel-ark (the configured tree 7.2.12-gcov was built from; /lib/modules/7.2.12-gcov/build does not exist here) with gcc 15.3.1 while the kernel was built with gcc 15.2.1 (kbuild's informational notice).

Procedure, in this order: stock, V0, V1, V2, then V0 reloaded and left loaded (the state found at the start). Per variant: unbind i2c-INT347E:00 from the ov7251 driver, sudo -n modprobe -r ov7251, sudo -n insmod <variant>/ov7251.ko (or sudo -n modprobe ov7251 for stock), read /sys/module/ov7251/taint, wait for the sensor entity (conftest.subdev()), then python3 tools/link-stress.py --label <name> --runs 3 --frames 150 --fps 30 --out /tmp/claude-1000/-home-antoine-projects-surface/3ccf287b-d9c6-4190-a42c-0b614d1d1d83/scratchpad/link-stress-results.jsonl (its readback block, read over I2C while streaming, is the proof of which table runs); for V1 and V2 also pytest -q tests/test_k3_timing.py tests/test_k11_strobe_registers.py tests/test_k12_subdev_state.py; after each variant journalctl -k --since <variant start> filtered for WARNING, BUG, Oops, lockdep, "Call Trace". Expected readbacks: stock 0x30b4=0x03 0x30b3=0x4b 0x30b1=0x01, link_frequency 240000000; V0 0x30b4=0x01 0x30b3=0x85 0x30b1=0x04 0x4837=0x19, link_frequency 319200000; V1 0x30b4=0x04 0x30b3=0x85 0x30b1=0x01 0x4837=0x19; V2 like V1 with 0x4837=0x1f. Each command below is shown as "$ command", followed by its combined stdout+stderr and "[exit N]".

