## Variant: V3 (sudo -n insmod /tmp/claude-1000/-home-antoine-projects-surface/3ccf287b-d9c6-4190-a42c-0b614d1d1d83/scratchpad/variants/V3/ov7251.ko), start 2026-10-27 21:20:19

V3 = kernel/backport/ov7251.c (V0) with .mipi_div = 0x01 (was 0x05) in the ov7251_pll1_cfg_19_2_mhz_319_2_mhz initializer and nothing else: the complete PLL1 setting of the Windows driver's first mode table (pre_div 0x01, mult 0x85, div 0x04, pix_div 0x0a, mipi_div 0x01) and what D. Manresa tried on his Surface Pro 7+, where it made the link far worse. The datasheet says register 0x30b5 (MIPI divider) values other than 2 and 4 all mean "divide by 1", so on paper V3 runs the same clocks as V0 and should behave like it. Built exactly like V0, V1 and V2 (same Makefile, same unchanged ipu-bridge.c, make -s against /home/antoine/build/kernel-gcov/kernel-ark because /lib/modules/7.2.12-gcov/build does not exist here, gcc 15.3.1 against the kernel's 15.2.1): /tmp/claude-1000/-home-antoine-projects-surface/3ccf287b-d9c6-4190-a42c-0b614d1d1d83/scratchpad/variants/V3/ov7251.ko, sha256 e2307c6437fbb862f954900c0d9c4e5d81ea47105e677503d79715527f4ea5b7, vermagic "7.2.12-gcov SMP preempt mod_unload ". Expected readback: V0's with 0x30b5=0x01, i.e. 0x30b4=0x01 0x30b3=0x85 0x30b1=0x04 0x30b5=0x01 0x4837=0x19, link_frequency 319200000. Procedure as above: build, K9 reload (unbind, modprobe -r, insmod), taint, entity, link-stress.py --label V3 --runs 3 --frames 150 --fps 30, journalctl since the start, then V0 reloaded and left loaded with a 1-run, 30-frame link-stress.py --label final2. No pytest for V3 (not requested).

